5G lamp: colours for 4G and 4G+, chosen on the page

The 5G lamp showed the 5G type only - blue for SA, green for NSA - and stayed dark on
4G. It now shows every network type, in colours set on the LED page:

  4G  (LTE)                              red     (default)
  4G+ (LTE with carrier aggregation)     yellow  (red + green)
  5G NSA                                 green
  5G SA                                  blue
  3G, no service                         off, as before

- Each type can take off, red, green, blue, or a mix of two or three of the lamp's LEDs:
  yellow (red + green), cyan (green + blue), purple (red + blue), white (all three).
  set_tricolor lights the members of a mix together, cw_led_tricolor_color reads a mix
  back for the live card, and the card's lamp and channel dots draw it.
- 4G+ comes from AT+QCAINFO: one or more "SCC" lines on an LTE band. That is the rule
  3gInfo-lite's radio page uses, so the lamp agrees with that page. It is asked only on
  LTE, once per modem poll, and not at all when 4G and 4G+ share a colour. A QCAINFO read
  that fails or comes back cut short keeps the previous answer, so a contended AT port does
  not flip the lamp between 4G and 4G+.
- The colours live in `config led 'fiveg'` (color_lte, color_lte_ca, color_nsa,
  color_sa). An unknown value falls back to the default. 90-cw-led adds the section once
  to a config written before this, with the defaults above.
- The contention grace now holds any network-type colour, not only blue and green.
- A solid red on the 5G lamp now means 4G; the 1 Hz red flash still means the first modem
  read is running.

Applies to: https://github.com/Pr0Luci/luci-app-cw-led.git @ a65586cf, after 0001 and 0002.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

